   "he": "וּכְקֶרֶן כַּרְכּוֹם. תָּנָא: לַח, וְלֹא יָבֵשׁ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches, with regard to the colors of impure blood: «And» what is the color that is «like the bright» color of the «crocus» flower that is impure? It is like the brightest part of the flower, which is used to produce the orange-colored spice saffron. The Sages «taught:» This is referring to the appearance of «moist» saffron that is still fresh «and not» to its «dry» counterpart."
